ilure summary\\n\\nThe native test `SunReflectionFactoryHelperTest.createsInstanceWithoutRunningTargetConstructor()` failed while Spring's bundled Objenesis implementation invoked a constructor created through `sun.reflect.ReflectionFactory`. Native Image reported a `MissingReflectionRegistrationError` for `java.lang.Object()`; the outer `tckTest` failure only propagated this single `nativeTest` failure.\\n\\n## Root cause and intervention\\n\\nThis is not a remaining metadata gap. The test requires `SunReflectionFactoryInstantiator` to synthesize a serialization constructor and instantiate an object without running its declared constructor. That VM-specific constructor-bypass path is unsupported native-image behavior.\\n\\nThe Codex repair repeatedly registered `java.lang.Object()`—including unconditionally—and also registered the target test type for serialization, but the same runtime failure remained. More reachability metadata therefore cannot preserve this behavior. The generated `SunReflectionFactoryHelperTest.java` was removed, and no metadata file was changed during this intervention.\\n\\n## Preserved support\\n\\nThe remaining generated suite should be preserved because all other 27 native tests passed. They continue to exercise Spring Core annotation synthesis and mapping, class and reflection utilities, class-loader behavior, classpath resources, resource URL handling, and VFS integration. Removing only the unsupported constructor-bypass test retains broad, meaningful metadata validation for the library. §FS-repository-functional-spec.5.2\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n`./gradlew test -Pcoordinates=org.springframework:spring-core:5.3.15 --quiet` passed after the test was removed: 27 tests started and 27 succeeded.\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
